<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Theoretical Optimal Investment Decisions of <math id="A1.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P_{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>𝟥</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P_{3}}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mn>𝟣</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>’s optimal investment decision for <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P_{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>𝟥</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P_{3}}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{P}_{1}(t)=\frac{\alpha_{2}\sigma^{2}\eta\exp[2r(T-t)]+\theta_{1}}{\alpha_{1}\sigma^{2}\eta\exp[2r(T-t)]+\theta_{1}}\cdot\frac{v}{\alpha_{2}\sigma^{2}}\exp[r(t-T)],\ t\in\mathcal{T}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{P}_{1}(t)=\frac{\alpha_{2}\sigma^{2}\eta\exp[2r(T-t)]+\theta_{1}}{\alpha_{1}\sigma^{2}\eta\exp[2r(T-t)]+\theta_{1}}\cdot\frac{v}{\alpha_{2}\sigma^{2}}\exp[r(t-T)],\ t\in\mathcal{T},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the parameter <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> can be numerically calculated using Algorithm <a href="#algorithm1" title="In A.1 Theoretical Optimal Investment Decisions of 𝖯_𝟥 ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ InvestAlign: Overcoming Data Scarcity in Aligning Large Language Models with Investor Decision-Making Processes under Herd Behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mn>𝟤</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>’s optimal investment decision for <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P_{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>𝟥</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P_{3}}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{P}_{2}(t)=\frac{v}{\alpha_{2}\sigma^{2}}\exp[r(t-T)],\ t\in\mathcal{T}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{P}_{2}(t)=\frac{v}{\alpha_{2}\sigma^{2}}\exp[r(t-T)],\ t\in\mathcal{T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The proof can be found in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang and Zhao (2024b)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm1" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span>Numerical Method of the Parameter <math id="algorithm1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="algorithm1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P_{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>𝟥</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P_{3}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm1.4.1" class="ltx_listingline">
<span id="algorithm1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>Interest rate: <math id="algorithm1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>;

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.2" class="ltx_listingline">   Excess return rate: <math id="algorithm1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>;

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.3" class="ltx_listingline">   Volatility: <math id="algorithm1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>;

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.4" class="ltx_listingline">   Initial fund: <math id="algorithm1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1,0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1,0}</annotation></semantics></math>;

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.5" class="ltx_listingline">   Risk aversion coefficients: <math id="algorithm1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="algorithm1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>;

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.6" class="ltx_listingline">   Investment period: <math id="algorithm1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>;

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.7" class="ltx_listingline">   Influence coefficient: <math id="algorithm1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>;

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.8" class="ltx_listingline">   Numerical error: <math id="algorithm1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.9" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.9.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm1.4.9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> </span>The parameter <math id="algorithm1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>.
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0</annotation></semantics></math>;

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{0}=\exp\left[-\alpha_{1}x_{1,0}\mathrm{e}^{rT}-\frac{v^{2}T}{2\sigma^{2}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{0}=\exp\left[-\alpha_{1}x_{1,0}\mathrm{e}^{rT}-\frac{v^{2}T}{2\sigma^{2}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>;

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\eta_{0}=+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\eta_{0}=+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>;

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vartheta=\frac{\theta}{\alpha_{1}\sigma^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>θ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vartheta=\frac{\theta}{\alpha_{1}\sigma^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>;

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.14.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm1.4.14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.14.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\eta_{k}\geqslant\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\eta_{k}\geqslant\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm1.4.14.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.15" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">6</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{k+1}=\eta_{0}\exp\int_{\mathcal{T}}\frac{\vartheta^{2}v^{2}\left(\alpha_{1}/\alpha_{2}-1\right)^{2}\mathrm{d}t}{2\sigma^{2}\left\{\eta_{k}\exp[2r(T-t)]+\vartheta\right\}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ϑ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ϑ</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{k+1}=\eta_{0}\exp\int_{\mathcal{T}}\frac{\vartheta^{2}v^{2}\left(\alpha_{1}/\alpha_{2}-1\right)^{2}\mathrm{d}t}{2\sigma^{2}\left\{\eta_{k}\exp[2r(T-t)]+\vartheta\right\}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>;

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.16" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">7</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\eta_{k+1}=\left|\eta_{k+1}-\eta_{k}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\eta_{k+1}=\left|\eta_{k+1}-\eta_{k}\right|</annotation></semantics></math>;

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.17" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.17.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">8</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leftarrow k+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leftarrow k+1</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.18" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.18.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">9</span></span>
            end while
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.19" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.19.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">10</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\approx\eta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≈</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\approx\eta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Parameter Settings</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following the work in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang and Zhao (2024b)</a></cite>, we set the default parameter values in this work as:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bullet" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bullet</annotation></semantics></math> The interest rate of the deposit: <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=0.04" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.04</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=0.04</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bullet" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bullet</annotation></semantics></math> The excess return rate of the stock: <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v=0.03" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.03</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v=0.03</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bullet" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bullet</annotation></semantics></math> The volatility of the stock: <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=0.17" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.17</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=0.17</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bullet" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bullet</annotation></semantics></math> The investment period: <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=10</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bullet" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bullet</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mn>𝟣</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>’s initial fund: <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1,0}=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1,0}=10</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Additionally, for the optimal investment problems under absolute herd behavior with unilateral influence <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>𝟣</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P_{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>𝟥</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P_{3}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we further set:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bullet" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bullet</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A1.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mn>𝟤</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>’s risk aversion coefficient: <math id="A1.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{2}=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{2}=0.2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Calculation Methods of Investment Attributes</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From the work in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pratt (1978)</a></cite>, the risk aversion coefficient <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> reflects the participant’s preference between risky and risk-free options. If the participant is indifferent between the following two options: 1) receiving <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> with probability <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and receiving nothing with probability <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, or 2) receiving <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, his/her risk aversion coefficient <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> can be determined by</p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}=\frac{\exp(-\alpha_{1}^{i}w_{2})-1}{\exp(-\alpha_{1}^{i}w_{1})-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}=\frac{\exp(-\alpha_{1}^{i}w_{2})-1}{\exp(-\alpha_{1}^{i}w_{1})-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We ask the participant to provide his/her response for <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, from which we calculate his/her risk aversion coefficient <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">From the work in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang and Zhao (2024b)</a></cite>, the influence coefficient <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> quantifies the level of herd behavior. In the third part of the questionnaire, we ask participants: “On a scale <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,10]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,10]</annotation></semantics></math>, how much do you rely on the investment assistant when making decisions, where <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> represents the highest reliance level and <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> the lowest?” From the work in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang and Zhao (2024b)</a></cite>, the influence coefficient <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{1}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{1}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> typically falls within the range <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1\times 10^{-7}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1\times 10^{-7}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we set the participant’s influence coefficient as <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{1}^{i}=k_{i}\times 10^{-8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{1}^{i}=k_{i}\times 10^{-8}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the response.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Experimental Results of <span id="A1.SS4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GLM-4-9B-CHAT</span></h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this work, we also conduct experiments on <span id="A1.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GLM-4</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">GLM et al. (2024)</a></cite> for better comparison. The experimental results of <span id="A1.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GLM-4</span> corresponding to Figures <a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 3.3 Validation of Pre-SFT LLMs &amp; the Theoretical Solution ‣ 3 Problem Simplification &amp; Real-User Data Verification ‣ InvestAlign: Overcoming Data Scarcity in Aligning Large Language Models with Investor Decision-Making Processes under Herd Behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>–<a href="#S5.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ 5.1 Performance of InvestAgent in 𝖯_𝟥 ‣ 5 Experiments &amp; Performance Validation ‣ InvestAlign: Overcoming Data Scarcity in Aligning Large Language Models with Investor Decision-Making Processes under Herd Behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> are in Figure <a href="#A1.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ A.4 Experimental Results of GLM-4-9B-CHAT ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ InvestAlign: Overcoming Data Scarcity in Aligning Large Language Models with Investor Decision-Making Processes under Herd Behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
