<figure id="A1.F6.sf4" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2507.06528v1/invest_alpha0.6_theta7_glm_sft_notation.svg" id="A1.F6.sf4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:167/126;" width="167" height="126"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(d) </span>Figure <a href="#S5.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ 5.1 Performance of InvestAgent in 𝖯_𝟥 ‣ 5 Experiments &amp; Performance Validation ‣ InvestAlign: Overcoming Data Scarcity in Aligning Large Language Models with Investor Decision-Making Processes under Herd Behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>The experimental results of <span id="A1.F6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GLM-4</span> corresponding to Figures <a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 3.3 Validation of Pre-SFT LLMs &amp; the Theoretical Solution ‣ 3 Problem Simplification &amp; Real-User Data Verification ‣ InvestAlign: Overcoming Data Scarcity in Aligning Large Language Models with Investor Decision-Making Processes under Herd Behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>–<a href="#S5.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ 5.1 Performance of InvestAgent in 𝖯_𝟥 ‣ 5 Experiments &amp; Performance Validation ‣ InvestAlign: Overcoming Data Scarcity in Aligning Large Language Models with Investor Decision-Making Processes under Herd Behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The experimental results of <span id="A1.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GLM-4</span> in Figure <a href="#A1.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ A.4 Experimental Results of GLM-4-9B-CHAT ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ InvestAlign: Overcoming Data Scarcity in Aligning Large Language Models with Investor Decision-Making Processes under Herd Behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> are similar to those of <span id="A1.SS4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Qwen-2</span> and <span id="A1.SS4.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Llama-3.1</span>, and we omit the analysis here.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Comparison of Real-User Data and Pre-SFT LLMs’ Investment Decision on <math id="A1.SS5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>𝟣</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>𝟣</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From Figure <a href="#A1.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ A.5 Comparison of Real-User Data and Pre-SFT LLMs’ Investment Decision on 𝖯_𝟣 and 𝖯_𝟣 ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ InvestAlign: Overcoming Data Scarcity in Aligning Large Language Models with Investor Decision-Making Processes under Herd Behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, we can find that the performances of pre-SFT LLMs in <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>𝟣</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> are misaligned with real-user data.
Note that when <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mn>𝟤</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>’s influence coefficient <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{2}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the complex problem <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>𝟤</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> degenerates into the simple problem <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P_{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>𝟥</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P_{3}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, from Figure <a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 3.3 Validation of Pre-SFT LLMs &amp; the Theoretical Solution ‣ 3 Problem Simplification &amp; Real-User Data Verification ‣ InvestAlign: Overcoming Data Scarcity in Aligning Large Language Models with Investor Decision-Making Processes under Herd Behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we can also draw the conclusion that the performances of pre-SFT LLMs in <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>𝟤</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> are misaligned with real-user data.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F7" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A1.F7.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2507.06528v1/invest_alpha0.7_theta5_gpt_relative.svg" id="A1.F7.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:167/125;" width="167" height="125"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span><span id="A1.F7.sf1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GPT-3.5</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A1.F7.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2507.06528v1/invest_alpha0.7_theta8_glm_relative.svg" id="A1.F7.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:167/125;" width="167" height="125"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span><span id="A1.F7.sf2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GLM-4</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A1.F7.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2507.06528v1/invest_alpha0.7_theta5_qwen_relative.svg" id="A1.F7.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:167/125;" width="167" height="125"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span><span id="A1.F7.sf3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Qwen-2</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A1.F7.sf4" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2507.06528v1/invest_alpha0.7_theta5_llama_relative.svg" id="A1.F7.sf4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:167/125;" width="167" height="125"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(d) </span><span id="A1.F7.sf4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Llama-3.1</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>Comparison of real-user data (<math id="A1.F7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{P}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{P}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>) and pre-SFT LLMs’ investment decision (<math id="A1.F7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>) on <math id="A1.F7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>𝟣</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6 </span>Statistical Tests’ Results of the Differences and Correlation Coefficients</h3>

<div id="A1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define the difference <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and correlation coefficient <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> between <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\tilde{P}_{1}^{i}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\tilde{P}_{1}^{i}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\hat{P}_{1}^{i}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\hat{P}_{1}^{i}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}=\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}[\tilde{P}_{1}^{i}(t)-\hat{P}_{1}^{i}(t)]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}=\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}[\tilde{P}_{1}^{i}(t)-\hat{P}_{1}^{i}(t)],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{i}=\frac{\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}[\tilde{P}_{1}^{i}(t)-\bar{\tilde{P}}_{1}^{i}][\hat{P}_{1}^{i}(t)-\bar{\hat{P}}_{1}^{i}]}{\sqrt{\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}[\tilde{P}_{1}^{i}(t)-\bar{\tilde{P}}_{1}^{i}]^{2}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}[\hat{P}_{1}^{i}(t)-\bar{\hat{P}}_{1}^{i}]^{2}}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{i}=\frac{\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}[\tilde{P}_{1}^{i}(t)-\bar{\tilde{P}}_{1}^{i}][\hat{P}_{1}^{i}(t)-\bar{\hat{P}}_{1}^{i}]}{\sqrt{\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}[\tilde{P}_{1}^{i}(t)-\bar{\tilde{P}}_{1}^{i}]^{2}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}[\hat{P}_{1}^{i}(t)-\bar{\hat{P}}_{1}^{i}]^{2}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\tilde{P}}_{1}^{i}=\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\tilde{P}_{1}^{i}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\tilde{P}}_{1}^{i}=\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\tilde{P}_{1}^{i}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\hat{P}}_{1}^{i}=\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\hat{P}_{1}^{i}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\hat{P}}_{1}^{i}=\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\hat{P}_{1}^{i}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the differences <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{d_{i}\}_{i\in\mathcal{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{d_{i}\}_{i\in\mathcal{I}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the results show that their mean does not significantly deviate from <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> at the <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\%</annotation></semantics></math> significance level, with a <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\text{-statistic}=-1.075" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-statistic</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1.075</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\text{-statistic}=-1.075</annotation></semantics></math>. For the correlation coefficients <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\rho_{i}\}_{i\in\mathcal{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\rho_{i}\}_{i\in\mathcal{I}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the results show that their mean does not significantly deviate from <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.85" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.85</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.85</annotation></semantics></math> at the <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\%</annotation></semantics></math> significance level, with a <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\text{-statistic}=-0.843" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-statistic</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.843</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\text{-statistic}=-0.843</annotation></semantics></math>. Since a mean difference close to <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> indicates minimal discrepancy and a correlation coefficient close to <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.85" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.85</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.85</annotation></semantics></math> reflects a strong positive relationship, we show that there exists significant consistency between the theoretical solution and real-user data.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.7 </span>Probability Distribution Function of <math id="A1.SS7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mn>𝟣</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>’s Optimal Investment Decision of <math id="A1.SS7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P_{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>𝟥</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P_{3}}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A1.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We assume the parameters <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy two uniform distributions, denoted by <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U(\underline{\alpha},\overline{\alpha})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(\underline{\alpha},\overline{\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U(\underline{\theta},\overline{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(\underline{\theta},\overline{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. Therefore, their probability distribution functions are</p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\alpha_{1}}(x)=\frac{1}{\overline{\alpha}-\underline{\alpha}},\ x\in[\underline{\alpha},\overline{\alpha}],\ \text{and}\ f_{\theta_{1}}(x)=\frac{1}{\overline{\theta}-\underline{\theta}},\ x\in[\underline{\theta},\overline{\theta}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>and</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\alpha_{1}}(x)=\frac{1}{\overline{\alpha}-\underline{\alpha}},\ x\in[\underline{\alpha},\overline{\alpha}],\ \text{and}\ f_{\theta_{1}}(x)=\frac{1}{\overline{\theta}-\underline{\theta}},\ x\in[\underline{\theta},\overline{\theta}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS7.p1.2" class="ltx_p">From (<a href="#A1.E11" title="In A.1 Theoretical Optimal Investment Decisions of 𝖯_𝟥 ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ InvestAlign: Overcoming Data Scarcity in Aligning Large Language Models with Investor Decision-Making Processes under Herd Behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>), using the convolution formula <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rényi (2007)</a></cite>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\hat{P}_{1}(t)}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\hat{P}_{1}(t)}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\overline{\theta}-\underline{\theta}}\int_{\underline{\theta}}^{\overline{\theta}}f_{\alpha_{1}}\left(\frac{1}{\sigma^{2}\eta\exp[2r(T-t)]}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\overline{\theta}-\underline{\theta}}\int_{\underline{\theta}}^{\overline{\theta}}f_{\alpha_{1}}\left(\frac{1}{\sigma^{2}\eta\exp[2r(T-t)]}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left.\cdot\left\{\frac{\alpha_{2}\sigma^{2}\eta\exp[2r(T-t)]+y}{x}\cdot\frac{v}{\alpha_{2}\sigma^{2}}\exp[r(t-T)]-y\right\}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left.\cdot\left\{\frac{\alpha_{2}\sigma^{2}\eta\exp[2r(T-t)]+y}{x}\cdot\frac{v}{\alpha_{2}\sigma^{2}}\exp[r(t-T)]-y\right\}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\cdot\frac{\alpha_{2}\sigma^{2}\eta\exp[2r(T-t)]+y}{\sigma^{2}\eta\exp[2r(T-t)]x^{2}}\cdot\frac{v}{\alpha_{2}\sigma^{2}}\exp[r(t-T)]\mathrm{d}y." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\cdot\frac{\alpha_{2}\sigma^{2}\eta\exp[2r(T-t)]+y}{\sigma^{2}\eta\exp[2r(T-t)]x^{2}}\cdot\frac{v}{\alpha_{2}\sigma^{2}}\exp[r(t-T)]\mathrm{d}y.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS7.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Here, following the work in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang and Zhao (2024a)</a></cite>, we assume that <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> approximately remains constant when <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> change slightly. Because <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{P}_{1}(t)\in\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{P}_{1}(t)\in\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, we can rewrite (<a href="#A1.E17" title="In A.7 Probability Distribution Function of 𝖠_𝟣’s Optimal Investment Decision of 𝖯_𝟥 ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ InvestAlign: Overcoming Data Scarcity in Aligning Large Language Models with Investor Decision-Making Processes under Herd Behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) as</p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\hat{P}_{1}(t)}(x)\approx\frac{\min[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]\cdot\max[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]}{\max[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]-\min[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]}\cdot\frac{1}{x^{2}},\ x\in\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\hat{P}_{1}(t)}(x)\approx\frac{\min[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]\cdot\max[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]}{\max[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]-\min[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]}\cdot\frac{1}{x^{2}},\ x\in\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS7.p1.4" class="ltx_p">That is, <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mn>𝟣</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>’s theoretical optimal decision <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{P}_{1}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{P}_{1}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> approximately satisfies a Pareto distribution. To simplify the notation, we denote the normalization parameter as</p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=\frac{\min[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]\cdot\max[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]}{\max[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]-\min[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=\frac{\min[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]\cdot\max[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]}{\max[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]-\min[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.8 </span>Gradient Norms of the Loss Function</h3>

<div id="A1.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">First, we derive the expression of <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\tilde{P}_{1}(t)}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\tilde{P}_{1}(t)}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> from (<a href="#S4.E7" title="In 4.2 Analysis of Parameter Convergence Rates ‣ 4 Methodology: InvestAlign ‣ InvestAlign: Overcoming Data Scarcity in Aligning Large Language Models with Investor Decision-Making Processes under Herd Behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>). Using the convolution formula in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rényi (2007)</a></cite>, we can obtain</p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\tilde{P}_{1}(t)}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\tilde{P}_{1}(t)}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\frac{1}{2\varepsilon}\int_{-\varepsilon}^{\varepsilon}f_{\hat{P}_{1}(t)}(x-y)\mathrm{d}y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mi>ε</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\frac{1}{2\varepsilon}\int_{-\varepsilon}^{\varepsilon}f_{\hat{P}_{1}(t)}(x-y)\mathrm{d}y</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\{\begin{aligned} &amp;\frac{c}{2\varepsilon}\int_{\min[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]-x}^{\varepsilon}\frac{1}{(x-y)^{2}}\mathrm{d}y,&amp;x\in[\min[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]-\varepsilon,\min[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]+\varepsilon)\\
&amp;\frac{c}{2\varepsilon}\int_{-\varepsilon}^{\varepsilon}\frac{1}{(x-y)^{2}}\mathrm{d}y,&amp;x\in[\min[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]+\varepsilon,\max[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]-\varepsilon)\\
&amp;\frac{c}{2\varepsilon}\int_{-\varepsilon}^{\max[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]-x}\frac{1}{(x-y)^{2}}\mathrm{d}y,&amp;x\in[\max[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]-\varepsilon,\max[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]+\varepsilon]\\
\end{aligned}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>ε</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>min</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>min</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mi>ε</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>min</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>max</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\{\begin{aligned} &amp;\frac{c}{2\varepsilon}\int_{\min[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]-x}^{\varepsilon}\frac{1}{(x-y)^{2}}\mathrm{d}y,&amp;x\in[\min[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]-\varepsilon,\min[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]+\varepsilon)\\
&amp;\frac{c}{2\varepsilon}\int_{-\varepsilon}^{\varepsilon}\frac{1}{(x-y)^{2}}\mathrm{d}y,&amp;x\in[\min[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]+\varepsilon,\max[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]-\varepsilon)\\
&amp;\frac{c}{2\varepsilon}\int_{-\varepsilon}^{\max[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]-x}\frac{1}{(x-y)^{2}}\mathrm{d}y,&amp;x\in[\max[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]-\varepsilon,\max[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)]+\varepsilon]\\
\end{aligned}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{c}{2\varepsilon}\left(\frac{1}{\max\{\min[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)],x-\varepsilon\}}-\frac{1}{\min\{\max[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)],x+\varepsilon\}}\right),\ x\in\tilde{\mathcal{P}}(t)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{c}{2\varepsilon}\left(\frac{1}{\max\{\min[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)],x-\varepsilon\}}-\frac{1}{\min\{\max[\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)],x+\varepsilon\}}\right),\ x\in\tilde{\mathcal{P}}(t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS8.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Next, we calculate the gradient norms. We have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla\hat{L}(\mathbf{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla\hat{L}(\mathbf{w})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\int_{\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)}f_{\hat{P}_{1}(t)}(x)\nabla\ln f_{P_{1}(t)}(x)\mathrm{d}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ln</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\int_{\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)}f_{\hat{P}_{1}(t)}(x)\nabla\ln f_{P_{1}(t)}(x)\mathrm{d}x</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\int_{\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)}\frac{f_{\hat{P}_{1}(t)}(x)}{f_{P_{1}(t)}(x)}\nabla\mathrm{Sigmoid}(\mathbf{z})\mathrm{d}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>Sigmoid</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\int_{\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)}\frac{f_{\hat{P}_{1}(t)}(x)}{f_{P_{1}(t)}(x)}\nabla\mathrm{Sigmoid}(\mathbf{z})\mathrm{d}x</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbf{z}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\int_{\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)}f_{\hat{P}_{1}(t)}(x)[1-f_{P_{1}(t)}(x)]\mathrm{d}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbf{z}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\int_{\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)}f_{\hat{P}_{1}(t)}(x)[1-f_{P_{1}(t)}(x)]\mathrm{d}x</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbf{z}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\left[\int_{\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)}f_{\hat{P}_{1}(t)}(x)\mathrm{d}x-\int_{\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)}f_{\hat{P}_{1}(t)}(x)f_{P_{1}(t)}(x)\mathrm{d}x\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbf{z}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\left[\int_{\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)}f_{\hat{P}_{1}(t)}(x)\mathrm{d}x-\int_{\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)}f_{\hat{P}_{1}(t)}(x)f_{P_{1}(t)}(x)\mathrm{d}x\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbf{z}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\left[1-\int_{\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)}f_{\hat{P}_{1}(t)}(x)f_{P_{1}(t)}(x)\mathrm{d}x\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbf{z}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\left[1-\int_{\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)}f_{\hat{P}_{1}(t)}(x)f_{P_{1}(t)}(x)\mathrm{d}x\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS8.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Therefore, the gradient norm is</p>
<table id="A1.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla\hat{L}(\mathbf{w})\|=\|\mathbf{z}\|\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\left[1-\int_{\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)}f_{\hat{P}_{1}(t)}(x)f_{P_{1}(t)}(x)\mathrm{d}x\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla\hat{L}(\mathbf{w})\|=\|\mathbf{z}\|\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\left[1-\int_{\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)}f_{\hat{P}_{1}(t)}(x)f_{P_{1}(t)}(x)\mathrm{d}x\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS8.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Using the same method as above, we can obtain</p>
<table id="A1.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla\tilde{L}(\mathbf{w})\|=\|\mathbf{z}\|\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\left[1-\int_{\tilde{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)}f_{\tilde{P}_{1}(t)}(x)f_{P_{1}(t)}(x)\mathrm{d}x\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla\tilde{L}(\mathbf{w})\|=\|\mathbf{z}\|\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\left[1-\int_{\tilde{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)}f_{\tilde{P}_{1}(t)}(x)f_{P_{1}(t)}(x)\mathrm{d}x\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS8.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Then, we compare the two gradient norms <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla\hat{L}(\mathbf{w})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla\hat{L}(\mathbf{w})\|</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla\tilde{L}(\mathbf{w})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla\tilde{L}(\mathbf{w})\|</annotation></semantics></math>. From (<a href="#A1.E22" title="In A.8 Gradient Norms of the Loss Function ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ InvestAlign: Overcoming Data Scarcity in Aligning Large Language Models with Investor Decision-Making Processes under Herd Behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>) and (<a href="#A1.E23" title="In A.8 Gradient Norms of the Loss Function ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ InvestAlign: Overcoming Data Scarcity in Aligning Large Language Models with Investor Decision-Making Processes under Herd Behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>), we only need to compare the following two integrals:</p>
<table id="A1.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{I}=\int_{\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)}f_{\hat{P}_{1}(t)}(x)f_{P_{1}(t)}(x)\mathrm{d}x," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{I}=\int_{\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)}f_{\hat{P}_{1}(t)}(x)f_{P_{1}(t)}(x)\mathrm{d}x,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS8.p1.6" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A1.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{I}=\int_{\tilde{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)}f_{\tilde{P}_{1}(t)}(x)f_{P_{1}(t)}(x)\mathrm{d}x." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{I}=\int_{\tilde{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)}f_{\tilde{P}_{1}(t)}(x)f_{P_{1}(t)}(x)\mathrm{d}x.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS8.p1.7" class="ltx_p">Because the investment decisions of the pre-SFT LLM can be arbitrary due to the randomness of model parameters, we have</p>
<table id="A1.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)\subset\tilde{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)\subset\mathcal{P}_{1}(t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)\subset\tilde{\mathcal{P}}_{1}(t)\subset\mathcal{P}_{1}(t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS8.p1.8" class="ltx_p">Because <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{P_{1}(t)}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{P_{1}(t)}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is monotonically decreasing, from (<a href="#S4.E7" title="In 4.2 Analysis of Parameter Convergence Rates ‣ 4 Methodology: InvestAlign ‣ InvestAlign: Overcoming Data Scarcity in Aligning Large Language Models with Investor Decision-Making Processes under Herd Behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) and (<a href="#A1.E21" title="In A.8 Gradient Norms of the Loss Function ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ InvestAlign: Overcoming Data Scarcity in Aligning Large Language Models with Investor Decision-Making Processes under Herd Behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>), we can prove that</p>
<table id="A1.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{I}&lt;\tilde{I}&lt;1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>&lt;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{I}&lt;\tilde{I}&lt;1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS8.p1.9" class="ltx_p">and thus we have</p>
<table id="A1.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla\hat{L}(\mathbf{w})\|&gt;\|\nabla\tilde{L}(\mathbf{w})\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla\hat{L}(\mathbf{w})\|&gt;\|\nabla\tilde{L}(\mathbf{w})\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS9" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.9 </span>The Ablation Study on the Hyper-parameters of SFT</h3>

<div id="A1.SS9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conduct an ablation study on the hyper-parameters of fine-tuning, including LoRA Rank and fine-tuning steps. Here, we take <span id="A1.SS9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Qwen-2</span> and <span id="A1.SS9.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Llama-3.1</span> in solving <math id="A1.SS9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P}_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P}_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> as examples. The experimental results are in Tables <a href="#A1.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ A.9 The Ablation Study on the Hyper-parameters of SFT ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ InvestAlign: Overcoming Data Scarcity in Aligning Large Language Models with Investor Decision-Making Processes under Herd Behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and Table <a href="#A1.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ A.9 The Ablation Study on the Hyper-parameters of SFT ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ InvestAlign: Overcoming Data Scarcity in Aligning Large Language Models with Investor Decision-Making Processes under Herd Behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. It can be seen that our <span id="A1.SS9.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">InvestAlign</span> consistently enhances the agreement between the <span id="A1.SS9.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">InvestAgent</span> and real-user data across various hyperparameters. Furthermore, the overall MSE decreases as the strength of fine-tuning increases, either through a larger LoRA Rank or more fine-tuning steps, underscoring the effectiveness of <span id="A1.SS9.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">InvestAlign</span>. We hypothesize that full-parameter fine-tuning could yield even better results if computational resources permit, which we plan to explore in future studies.</p>
</div>
