<td id="A1.T5.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:43.8pt;padding-right:43.8pt;">     3.97     </td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:43.8pt;padding-right:43.8pt;">     4.08     </td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T5.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T5.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r" style="padding-left:43.8pt;padding-right:43.8pt;">     <span id="A1.T5.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FinEval-SFT LLM</span>     </td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:43.8pt;padding-right:43.8pt;">     3.35     </td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:43.8pt;padding-right:43.8pt;">     3.28     </td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T5.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T5.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r" style="padding-left:43.8pt;padding-right:43.8pt;">     <span id="A1.T5.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ConvFinQA-SFT LLM</span>     </td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:43.8pt;padding-right:43.8pt;">     2.77     </td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:43.8pt;padding-right:43.8pt;">     1.96     </td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T5.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T5.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r" style="padding-left:43.8pt;padding-right:43.8pt;">     <span id="A1.T5.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">InvestAgent</span>     </td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:43.8pt;padding-right:43.8pt;">     <span id="A1.T5.2.6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2.16</span>     </td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:43.8pt;padding-right:43.8pt;">     <span id="A1.T5.2.6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1.59</span>     </td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T5.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T5.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:43.8pt;padding-right:43.8pt;" colspan="3">     <math id="A1.T5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>𝟣</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>: Relative herd behavior with unilateral influence (original complex problem)     </td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T5.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T5.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:43.8pt;padding-right:43.8pt;">     <span id="A1.T5.2.8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pre-SFT LLM</span>     </td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:43.8pt;padding-right:43.8pt;">     17.22     </td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:43.8pt;padding-right:43.8pt;">     13.07     </td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T5.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T5.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r" style="padding-left:43.8pt;padding-right:43.8pt;">     <span id="A1.T5.2.9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FinEval-SFT LLM</span>     </td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:43.8pt;padding-right:43.8pt;">     13.74     </td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.9.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:43.8pt;padding-right:43.8pt;">     11.16     </td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T5.2.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T5.2.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r" style="padding-left:43.8pt;padding-right:43.8pt;">     <span id="A1.T5.2.10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ConvFinQA-SFT LLM</span>     </td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:43.8pt;padding-right:43.8pt;">     10.86     </td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.10.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:43.8pt;padding-right:43.8pt;">     9.61     </td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T5.2.11" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T5.2.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r" style="padding-left:43.8pt;padding-right:43.8pt;">     <span id="A1.T5.2.11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">InvestAgent</span>     </td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b" style="padding-left:43.8pt;padding-right:43.8pt;">     <span id="A1.T5.2.11.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">7.46</span>     </td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.11.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b" style="padding-left:43.8pt;padding-right:43.8pt;">     <span id="A1.T5.2.11.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">7.25</span>     </td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Comparison of the overall MSE between pre-SFT LLMs’, FinEval-SFT LLMs’, ConvFinQA-SFT LLMs’ and <span id="A1.T5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">InvestAgent</span>s’ investment decisions with real-user data.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS11.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS11.p2.1" class="ltx_p">From Table <a href="#A1.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ A.11 The Experimental Results of Compare InvestAgents with LLMs Fine-tuned Using the Baseline FinGPT Dataset ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ InvestAlign: Overcoming Data Scarcity in Aligning Large Language Models with Investor Decision-Making Processes under Herd Behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, it can be seen that <span id="A1.SS11.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">InvestAgent</span>s outperform the LLMs fine-tuned on the FinGPT datasets. This is because <span id="A1.SS11.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">InvestAgent</span>’s training dataset is specifically constructed for studying optimal investment problems with herding behavior, whereas FinGPT is more general. Therefore, <span id="A1.SS11.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">InvestAgent</span> shows better performance in the context of optimal investment analysis.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS12" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.12 </span>The Experimental Results of Validating that <span id="A1.SS12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">InvestAgent</span>s Better Reflect Economic Principles in the Presence of Investor Herd Behavior Compared to Pre-SFT LLMs</h3>

<section id="A1.SS12.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.12.1 </span>Experimental Setup</h4>

<div id="A1.SS12.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS12.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conduct experiments to validate whether <span id="A1.SS12.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">InvestAgent</span>s better reflect established economic principles in scenarios involving investor herd behavior compared to pre-SFT LLMs. Our analysis focuses on two foundational economic hypotheses:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS12.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mn>𝟣</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>: In both unilateral and mutual influence scenarios, as the influence coefficient increases, which amplifies herd behavior, agents’ investment decisions, i.e., <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P_{1}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P_{1}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P_{2}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P_{2}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>, will exhibit progressive convergence <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang and Zhao (2024a)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang and Zhao (2024b)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang and Zhao (2025)</a></cite>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mn>𝟤</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>: In the mutual influence scenario, as the influence coefficient increases, which amplifies herd behavior, the mean of the sum of the two agents’ terminal funds, i.e., <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[X_{1}(T)+X_{2}(T)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[X_{1}(T)+X_{2}(T)]</annotation></semantics></math>, will decrease <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Avery and Zemsky (1998)</a></cite>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS12.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS12.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We choose <math id="A1.SS12.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mn>𝟣</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>’s influence coefficient <math id="A1.SS12.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A1.SS12.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathcal{S}}_{\theta_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{S}}_{\theta_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A1.SS12.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{S}}_{\theta_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{S}}_{\theta_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS12.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>𝟣</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS12.SSS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P_{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>𝟥</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P_{3}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and set the homogeneous influence coefficients of both <math id="A1.SS12.SSS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mn>𝟣</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS12.SSS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mn>𝟤</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS12.SSS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{1}=\theta_{2}:=\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{1}=\theta_{2}:=\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, from <math id="A1.SS12.SSS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathcal{S}}_{\theta_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{S}}_{\theta_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A1.SS12.SSS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{S}}_{\theta_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{S}}_{\theta_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS12.SSS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>𝟤</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Other parameters are specified in Appendix <a href="#A1.SS2" title="A.2 Parameter Settings ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ InvestAlign: Overcoming Data Scarcity in Aligning Large Language Models with Investor Decision-Making Processes under Herd Behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>. We generate corresponding prompts and collect <span id="A1.SS12.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">InvestAgent</span>s’ responses, from which we extract <math id="A1.SS12.SSS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mn>𝟣</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>’s investment decision <math id="A1.SS12.SSS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P_{1}^{\mathrm{SFT}}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>SFT</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P_{1}^{\mathrm{SFT}}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS12.SSS1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>𝟣</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS12.SSS1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P_{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>𝟥</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P_{3}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and both <math id="A1.SS12.SSS1.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mn>𝟣</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>’s investment decision <math id="A1.SS12.SSS1.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P_{1}^{\mathrm{SFT}}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>SFT</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P_{1}^{\mathrm{SFT}}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS12.SSS1.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mn>𝟤</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>’s investment decision <math id="A1.SS12.SSS1.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P_{2}^{\mathrm{SFT}}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>SFT</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P_{2}^{\mathrm{SFT}}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS12.SSS1.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>𝟤</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS12.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.12.2 </span>Validation of <math id="A1.SS12.SSS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mn>𝟣</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="A1.SS12.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS12.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A1.SS12.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>𝟣</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS12.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P_{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>𝟥</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P_{3}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we plot <math id="A1.SS12.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mn>𝟣</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>’s decisions <math id="A1.SS12.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P_{1}^{\mathrm{SFT}}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>SFT</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P_{1}^{\mathrm{SFT}}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> under different influence coefficients <math id="A1.SS12.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. To facilitate comparison of the herd behavior’s impact on investment decisions, we simultaneously plot <math id="A1.SS12.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mn>𝟤</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>’s optimal decision <math id="A1.SS12.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\hat{P}_{2}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\hat{P}_{2}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> calculated from (<a href="#A1.E12" title="In A.1 Theoretical Optimal Investment Decisions of 𝖯_𝟥 ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ InvestAlign: Overcoming Data Scarcity in Aligning Large Language Models with Investor Decision-Making Processes under Herd Behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>). Additionally, we also show the results of real-user data for comparison. The experimental results are in Figure <a href="#A1.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ A.12.2 Validation of 𝖧_𝟣 ‣ A.12 The Experimental Results of Validating that InvestAgents Better Reflect Economic Principles in the Presence of Investor Herd Behavior Compared to Pre-SFT LLMs ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ InvestAlign: Overcoming Data Scarcity in Aligning Large Language Models with Investor Decision-Making Processes under Herd Behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> and Figure <a href="#A1.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ A.12.2 Validation of 𝖧_𝟣 ‣ A.12 The Experimental Results of Validating that InvestAgents Better Reflect Economic Principles in the Presence of Investor Herd Behavior Compared to Pre-SFT LLMs ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ InvestAlign: Overcoming Data Scarcity in Aligning Large Language Models with Investor Decision-Making Processes under Herd Behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, respectively. From Figure <a href="#A1.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ A.12.2 Validation of 𝖧_𝟣 ‣ A.12 The Experimental Results of Validating that InvestAgents Better Reflect Economic Principles in the Presence of Investor Herd Behavior Compared to Pre-SFT LLMs ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ InvestAlign: Overcoming Data Scarcity in Aligning Large Language Models with Investor Decision-Making Processes under Herd Behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> and Figure <a href="#A1.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ A.12.2 Validation of 𝖧_𝟣 ‣ A.12 The Experimental Results of Validating that InvestAgents Better Reflect Economic Principles in the Presence of Investor Herd Behavior Compared to Pre-SFT LLMs ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ InvestAlign: Overcoming Data Scarcity in Aligning Large Language Models with Investor Decision-Making Processes under Herd Behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, we observe that as the influence coefficient <math id="A1.SS12.SSS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> increases, <math id="A1.SS12.SSS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mn>𝟣</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>’s decision <math id="A1.SS12.SSS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P_{1}^{\mathrm{SFT}}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>SFT</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P_{1}^{\mathrm{SFT}}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> gradually converges toward <math id="A1.SS12.SSS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mn>𝟤</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>’s optimal decision <math id="A1.SS12.SSS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\hat{P}_{2}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\hat{P}_{2}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS12.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS12.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A1.SS12.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>𝟤</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we plot both <math id="A1.SS12.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mn>𝟣</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>’s decisions <math id="A1.SS12.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P_{1}^{\mathrm{SFT}}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>SFT</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P_{1}^{\mathrm{SFT}}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS12.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mn>𝟤</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>’s decisions <math id="A1.SS12.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P_{2}^{\mathrm{SFT}}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>SFT</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P_{2}^{\mathrm{SFT}}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> under different influence coefficients <math id="A1.SS12.SSS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> in Figure <a href="#A1.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ A.12.2 Validation of 𝖧_𝟣 ‣ A.12 The Experimental Results of Validating that InvestAgents Better Reflect Economic Principles in the Presence of Investor Herd Behavior Compared to Pre-SFT LLMs ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ InvestAlign: Overcoming Data Scarcity in Aligning Large Language Models with Investor Decision-Making Processes under Herd Behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>. From Figure <a href="#A1.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ A.12.2 Validation of 𝖧_𝟣 ‣ A.12 The Experimental Results of Validating that InvestAgents Better Reflect Economic Principles in the Presence of Investor Herd Behavior Compared to Pre-SFT LLMs ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ InvestAlign: Overcoming Data Scarcity in Aligning Large Language Models with Investor Decision-Making Processes under Herd Behavior" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, we observe that increasing influence coefficients lead to progressive convergence between <math id="A1.SS12.SSS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mn>𝟣</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>’s decisions <math id="A1.SS12.SSS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P_{1}^{\mathrm{SFT}}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>SFT</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P_{1}^{\mathrm{SFT}}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS12.SSS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mn>𝟤</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>’s decisions <math id="A1.SS12.SSS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P_{2}^{\mathrm{SFT}}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>SFT</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P_{2}^{\mathrm{SFT}}(t)\}_{t\in\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS12.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS12.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In summary, the above experimental results are consistent with and validate the hypothesis <math id="A1.SS12.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mn>𝟣</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
